===Fraud allegations===
Despite the Provisional Election Council sanctioning the election, protests continued the next day. Almost two-thirds of the candidates also called for the election to be annulled alleging fraud and many voters being refused ballots.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|last=|first=|date=|title=Haiti vote chaos continues|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2010/11/29/haiti-vote-chaos-continues|access-date=2021-02-09|website=www.aljazeera.com|language=en}}</ref> Despite this, international election monitors declared the polls valid and said the results should not be invalidated.<ref name="DemocracyNow">{{Cite web|title=Election Monitors OK Haiti Election|url=https://www.democracynow.org/2010/11/30/headlines/election_monitors_ok_haiti_election|access-date=2021-02-09|website=Democracy Now!|language=en}}</ref> This opinion was not shared by the [[Organization of American States|OAS]] and the [[Caribbean Community|CARICOM]] who, after a preliminary report, said that there many problems surrounding the election.{{Clarify|date=April 2011}}<ref>{{Cite news|last=|first=|date=2011-04-21|title=The OAS-CARICOM Joint Mission has taken note of the publication of the final results of the second round of the presidential and legislative elections in Haiti|url=https://www.oas.org/en/media_center/press_release.asp?scodigo=e-639/11|access-date=2021-02-09|website=OAS - Organization of American States|language=en}}</ref> Following further protests by several candidates, the UN called for calm and urged candidates to call on their supporters not to instigate trouble. It also said that a deteriorating security situation could undermine containment of the cholera epidemic.<ref name=":1" /> [[CBC News]] reporters also said that there was "massive fraud".<ref name="CBCNews">[https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/haiti-election-a-massive-fraud-1.941996 Haiti Election Massive Fraud] CBC World News, November 28, 2010</ref> Port-au-Prince had four consecutive days of protests.<ref name="TRNN">[http://therealnews.com/t2/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=31&Itemid=74&jumival=5953 Protests over Haiti poll turn violent] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170703103351/http://therealnews.com/t2/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=31&Itemid=74&jumival=5953 |date=2017-07-03 }} [[The Real News]] (TRNN), December 3, 2010 (video 2:28)</ref>

